          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Yes—your proposal gives a useful direction, provided the backward step retains the joint information acquired forward.\n\nI developed it in [Note34](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-6/03_volterra_coefficient_dynamics/01_cluster_gap_transport/02_complex_p_mellin/notes/34_VCD_GT_CM_TIME_ZERO_FORWARD_STATISTICS_20261118.md):\n\n- The existing complete \\(t=0\\) census implies **388 real, simple zeros**, using conjugation and singleton counts.\n- With a paid exterior bound, forward evolution gives a quantitative minimum-gap and lower-tail estimate.\n- There is a precise limitation: for the unchanged initial-\\(M\\) backward horizon\n  \\[\n  h=\\frac{D}{2(1-DM)},\\qquad (h-t)'=-2Fh^2.\n  \\]\n  Under the stated nonnegative-\\(M,F\\) hypotheses, forwarding exact data cannot improve the endpoint reached by that same comparison.\n\nThus the promising route is to propagate **joint forcing or neighboring-gap information**, then preserve it in the backward estimate. The earlier retained-forcing calculation provides a concrete conditional target: \\(F\\ge0.3\\) would leave margin \\(>0.00006246\\); that source bound remains unproved.\n\nSeparate internal reviews checked both developments. Research notes, progress, overview, plan and milestone records are updated; chat history is refreshed with final capture queued.\n\n**Next: [B] B09 r2 — Astra:** select and acquire the joint forward information needed for a net backward gain. The [continuation](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-6/03_volterra_coefficient_dynamics/01_cluster_gap_transport/02_complex_p_mellin/notes/33_VCD_GT_CM_RETAINED_FORCING_CONTINUATION_20261118.md) records the requirements."
            ]
