              "This sounds promising, I could see a recursive approach of obtaining improved statistics in the forward direction, using that to improve the bounds in the backward direction, and then repeating. Perhaps there is a way of viewing this in a continuous \"forward backward\" kind of way, where some statistical quantity is improved from both sides simultaneously.&#x20;\n\nPlease include these and any other recent results in the manuscript. Please focus on analytical or theoretical results, leaving any numerics for supporting evidence. Please develop the ideas systematically, and methodically derive all of the relevant results, maximizing the coherence of the development of ideas, and the elegance of the results. Save the pdf in the output folder, which is ignored by git.\n\nIf necessary, please update the research overview, plan and progress file to incorporate this new idea, then write a continuation note for the next session.\n\n\\\n"
